WHY AGPL-3.0
============

This project is not AGPL by preference; it is AGPL by obligation. The licence
of a combined work is decided by the strongest copyleft it links against, and
here that is Terracotta's AGPL-3.0.

    Component                        Licence        How it is used
    -------------------------------  -------------  --------------------------
    Terracotta (PCL-Community fork)  AGPL-3.0       linked statically
                                                    (Runtime/Terracotta/
                                                     libterracotta.a)
    Amethyst-iOS / PojavLauncher     GPL-3.0        JavaApp, native bridges,
                                                    patched LWJGL + GLFW
    EasyTier (burningtnt fork)       LGPL-3.0       inside Terracotta
    MobileGlues                      LGPL-2.1-only  renderer
                                                    (Runtime/Frameworks/
                                                     libmobileglues.dylib)
    LWJGL                            BSD-3-Clause   3.3.3 and 3.4.1 stacks
    OpenJDK (Temurin)                GPL-2.0 + CE   bundled JRE

GPL-3.0 code may be combined into an AGPL-3.0 work -- GPLv3 section 13 permits
exactly this -- and the result must be distributed under AGPL-3.0. That is what
this repository does.


CORRECTION TO EARLIER RELEASES
==============================

Earlier builds of the Android project shipped an LGPL-3.0 LICENSE file. That
was wrong in two ways: the tree already contained PojavLauncher core (GPL-3.0),
and it shipped libterracotta.so (AGPL-3.0). Both projects now carry AGPL-3.0,
which is what the combination has required all along.


MODIFICATIONS TO UPSTREAM SOURCES
=================================

No upstream source is vendored as a patched copy. Every modification is applied
at build time by a script under Scripts/, so the diff against upstream stays
readable and each patch fails loudly if upstream moves:

    Scripts/build-mobileglues.sh   15 patches. Mach-O has no
                                   __attribute__((alias)); ES 3.0 fallbacks for
                                   ES 3.2/3.1 entry points; integer vertex
                                   attribute signedness (Metal requires the
                                   signedness of a vertex format to match the
                                   shader declaration, GL does not); RTLD_SELF
                                   instead of the Android RTLD_DEFAULT constant
                                   in glXGetProcAddress.

    Scripts/build-terracotta.sh     5 patches. Pins EasyTier to the tag the
                                   repository declares; adds iOS to the
                                   InterfaceFilter branch (the macOS branch
                                   shells out to `networksetup`, which iOS does
                                   not have); exposes the HTTP control server
                                   and a single C entry point for Swift.

    Scripts/build-javaapp.sh       GLFW shims for LWJGL 3.4.1, and a null guard
                                   in glfwGetInputMode.

Running a script prints every patch it applied.


